ey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2b858e27a0bd663ede05b603bf8d8e00ea7c1921e3e8fc775da89fe905237022","event_uuid":"1f12e253-b334-41bf-a33c-2724d7915b9e","position":{"commit_sha":"b297367d11f42d10c621dbc4feb5d456bd157934","position":"1786919987080207573-1f12e253-b334-41bf-a33c-2724d7915b9e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"First mandatory plan review BLOCKED on two E4 compatibility omissions: moving the five functions would otherwise bypass tests that patch authorship.subprocess, and the internal verify_authorship_at_commit resolver path was not explicitly tied to the authorship module-global binding. Revised the plan to preserve both seams, expanded the name-string caller/monkeypatch census, pinned the exact Any-count oracle inherited from abasic-doddering-harrier, split compound ACs into executable checks, and added the new sibling module to file impact. Re-review is required before claim.","timestamp":1786843033556957001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD/GREEN evidence: cherry-picked implementation commit (one implementation attempt) into the isolated worktree. Happy structural contract moved RED -> GREEN; focused held-out oracle passed 47 unit tests plus 1 real-git bulk-parity integration test. Mutation check replaced one `_authorship.subprocess.run` lookup with a direct subprocess call: the unseen signed-resolver oracle correctly went RED (`resolver_calls` 1 != 2), then returned GREEN after restoration. Temporary structural test removed; worktree contains only the two planned source files. Structural ACs pass: authorship.py 454 LOC, authorship_resolution.py 367 LOC, five facade exports resolve, explicit Any count remains 2, focused mypy passes. `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass. Exact `make test` passes: 13,575 passed, 25 skipped, 288 deselected in 1:29:34.\n\nThe extras-enforced full command exposed one unrelated pre-existing flaky liveness defect after 13,582 passes: store-isolation child pytest reported `[100%]` but did not terminate before its 90s watchdog. Focused reproduction timed out in 105.55s; a later unchanged focused run passed in 1.49s, proving flakiness. Filed `grindable-deviant-angwantibo` (bf7c-333e-29b0-4ee4), linked discovered_from, with exact evidence and a no-retry root-cause plan. This ticket's changed authorship surface remained green throughout; no unrelated fix was added.","timestamp":1786879333814005001}],"created_at":1786597447143591001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"72126233-8423-4d8d-97f8-275672c97d75","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9efe-8e88-70b3-4984"},{"link_uuid":"c4b13edb-24bb-4604-ad27-945779c9712b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2029-873f-de0d-4799"},{"link_uuid":"1f12e253-b334-41bf-a33c-2724d7915b9e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"858e-25a9-c195-4392"}],"description":"## Context\nDiscovered while landing abasic-doddering-harrier. Annotating `repo_root` parameters caused formatter-required wrapping and moved `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` from 784 to 793 LOC against the hard 800 cap in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`. The prior change is correct and merged; this task buys back module-size headroom through a behavior-preserving split.\n\nRe-wrapping is not an alternative because `ruff format --check` enforces the current layout. Raising the cap is prohibited by project policy.\n\n## Plan\n- Create `src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py` for the existing git-ancestry/commit-resolution cluster: `resolve_event_commit`, `resolve_position_commit`, `build_ticket_position_commit_map`, `build_introducing_commit_map`, and `build_position_commit_map`. This is an existing call-graph seam of roughly 330 LOC, so the new module is above the 100-LOC floor while `authorship.py` returns to the 200-500 target band.\n- Import and re-export all five names from `authorship_resolution.py` in `authorship.py`, preserving the current `rebar.attest.authorship.<name>` paths used by production callers and tests.\n- Preserve the established subprocess monkeypatch seam explicitly without an import-time cycle. Each moved function that invokes git performs a lazy in-function `import rebar.attest.authorship as _authorship` immediately before the call, then uses `_authorship.subprocess.run(...)`. `authorship_resolution.py` has no top-level import back to `authorship.py`; the lazy lookup occurs only after package initialization and mirrors the existing lazy `tracker_dir` import pattern. Therefore `monkeypatch.setattr(authorship, \"subprocess\", ...)` still intercepts every moved git path. This is compatibility indirection only; git arguments, branches, timeouts, fallbacks, return values, and exception handling remain unchanged.\n- Preserve the internal spy path explicitly: `verify_authorship_at_commit._resolve` remains in `authorship.py` and continues its module-global lookup of `resolve_event_commit`. The module-level imported binding is the re-export, and replacing `authorship.resolve_event_commit` updates that same module dictionary entry, so existing counting spies remain observable.\n- Use Serena `find_referencing_symbols` on all five definitions, then use repository-wide `rg` for string-based `setattr`/`getattr`/parametrization sites that the LSP cannot resolve. The semantic census confirms production callers in `opcert.py`, `verify_authorship.py`, `verify_opcert.py`, `compact_txn.py`, and `compact.py`; direct test/helper callers include the authorship resolver/batching/performance suites, `_opcert_helpers.py`, and `test_opcert_storage.py`. The string sweep covers monkeypatch consumers in `test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py`, `test_authorship_resolver_git_flags.py`, `test_authorship_resolver_git_flags_heldout.py`, `test_identity_perf_1cc0.py`, `test_identity_ts2_09f9_heldout.py`, `test_verify_identity_a2c7_perf.py`, `test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py`, `test_compact_sweep_perf.py`, plus the integration bulk-parity test.\n- Move code without changing decision logic. The only edited lookup is the lazy compatibility indirection required to preserve the existing subprocess test seam.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test \"$(wc -l < src/rebar/attest/authorship.py)\" -le 500` exits 0.\n- [ ] `test \"$(wc -l < src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py)\" -ge 100` exits 0.\n- [ ] `python -c \"from rebar.attest import authorship; [getattr(authorship, n) for n in (\\\"resolve_event_commit\\\", \\\"resolve_position_commit\\\", \\\"build_ticket_position_commit_map\\\", \\\"build_introducing_commit_map\\\", \\\"build_position_commit_map\\\")]\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] `pytest -q tests/unit/test_authorship_resolver_git_flags.py tests/unit/test_authorship_resolver_git_flags_heldout.py tests/integration/test_authorship_resolver_bulk_parity.py` passes, proving the `authorship.subprocess` monkeypatch still intercepts every moved resolver path.\n- [ ] `pytest -q tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py tests/unit/test_identity_perf_1cc0.py tests/unit/test_identity_ts2_09f9_heldout.py tests/unit/test_verify_identity_a2c7_perf.py tests/unit/test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py tests/unit/test_compact_sweep_perf.py tests/unit/test_opcert_storage.py` passes, proving `authorship.<name>` consumers still exercise the re-exported production paths.\n- [ ] `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` reports no errors.\n- [ ] `test \"$(grep -rhE \":\\s*Any\\b|->\\s*Any\\b\" src/rebar/attest/*.py | wc -l | tr -d \" \")\" -eq 2` exits 0, preserving the two explicit trust-root boundary annotations.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `make test` passes.\n- [ ] `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1 pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` passes after installing the locked dev/reviewbot/ui extras, matching the CI pytest selection.\n\n## Non-overlap\nTouches `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py`, the new `src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py`, and focused tests only if the RED-first compatibility oracle requires one. The prerequisite abasic-doddering-harrier is merged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/attest/authorship.py","reason":"retain the public facade and compatibility monkeypatch seams while removing the moved resolution cluster"},{"path":"src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py","reason":"new sibling module for the existing git ancestry and commit resolution cluster"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2029-873f-de0d-4799"],["relates_to","858e-25a9-c195-4392"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e781a365-a012-4536-a1a5-54c268649b4c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"760f-608f-4c69-449a","ticket_type":"task","title":"Split authorship.py: 793/800 LOC, 7 lines of module-size headroom","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c4b13edb-24bb-4604-ad27-945779c9712b","895bfeae-a0a1-4981-80aa-07d711071f67","e5cefcd5-0401-4559-9561-d4755cda9a0c","ec6b80ab-8665-46fb-b4d0-6bda512ae882","b6cd64fe-b2ec-41f7-9567-d21c731f63a4","f569e88c-a94a-43ba-9ec3-4de4bdbded79","3e127b96-0164-409f-b50a-176a865e8e1f","e781a365-a012-4536-a1a5-54c268649b4c","2d3391